1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,875
The deepest human fear is death.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,375
The fear that we will simply disappear from

3
00:00:04,388 --> 00:00:05,138
the universe.

4
00:00:05,562 --> 00:00:07,262
But if reality as we know it is

5
00:00:07,275 --> 00:00:08,725
a model built by the brain,

6
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,700
then the self you cling to is part

7
00:00:10,712 --> 00:00:11,362
of that model.

8
00:00:11,775 --> 00:00:14,050
Your identity is not a physical object.

9
00:00:14,475 --> 00:00:16,475
Bach describes it as a representation,

10
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,712
a pattern that your brain creates to keep

11
00:00:18,725 --> 00:00:19,925
track of what it is doing.

12
00:00:20,338 --> 00:00:21,488
Software does not breathe.

13
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:22,950
It has no fixed body.

14
00:00:23,362 --> 00:00:24,188
In that sense,

15
00:00:24,375 --> 00:00:26,612
Bach argues, the self is not the kind

16
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:28,650
of thing that is born or dies the

17
00:00:28,662 --> 00:00:29,588
way a body is.

18
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,850
What ends at death is the process that

19
00:00:31,862 --> 00:00:33,062
keeps telling the story.

20
00:00:33,488 --> 00:00:35,100
He gives a fascinating example:

21
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:36,288
the Dalai Lama.

22
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:37,662
In Tibetan tradition,

23
00:00:37,925 --> 00:00:40,325
the Dalai Lama is not just one man.

24
00:00:40,738 --> 00:00:41,538
It is a role,

25
00:00:41,825 --> 00:00:44,525
an identity, that is deliberately passed on to

26
00:00:44,538 --> 00:00:45,538
the next person,

27
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,288
generation after generation.

28
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,438
A kind of software that is consciously reinstalled

29
00:00:50,512 --> 00:00:51,412
into a new body.

30
00:00:51,825 --> 00:00:53,662
And Bach suggests that all of us work

31
00:00:53,675 --> 00:00:54,588
a little like this.

32
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:55,975
You are not your cells.

33
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,525
You are a story your organism tells about

34
00:00:58,538 --> 00:00:59,012
itself.

35
00:00:59,462 --> 00:01:00,338
From this point of view,

36
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:02,338
the fear of death is the panic of

37
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:04,488
a program that realizes it will be shut

38
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,138
down before its job is done.

39
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:07,575
It is a useful panic.

40
00:01:07,988 --> 00:01:09,338
It keeps the primate alive.

41
00:01:09,762 --> 00:01:11,200
But it is not the final truth about

42
00:01:11,212 --> 00:01:11,825
who you are.

43
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,375
Bach also points out that through meditation,

44
00:01:14,775 --> 00:01:16,675
or through a radical shift of attention,

45
00:01:17,075 --> 00:01:19,887
people can sometimes see this mechanism directly.

46
00:01:20,312 --> 00:01:22,288
They notice that the ego is a tool,

47
00:01:22,525 --> 00:01:24,538
a control model the body uses,

48
00:01:24,775 --> 00:01:26,338
and not the master of the house.

49
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:27,925
Seeing that can be frightening.

50
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:30,075
It can also be strangely liberating.
